The results of the Whipple’s Index are high in all regions as well as at the national level.  There is
a major difference in the Western Area where the index is the lowest, indicating a lower incidence
of age heaping on digits ‘0’ and ‘5’.
A similar picture is portrayed by the Myer’s Index with the highest value being in the Eastern
Region.  The index in the Western Area Region is twice as low than that of the Eastern Region,
which suggests that age reporting in single years is more than twice as good in the Western Area
Region as in the Eastern Region.  Again, the results of the Bachi Index are highest in the Eastern
Region and lowest in the Western Area Region.
 19

